{{Short description|Meta-tracking of the International dollar against the US dollar}}
{{notice|This is a [[TALOD:Meta|meta page]]. It tracks the value of the fictional [[International dollar]] against the real-world [[W:United States dollar|US dollar]] for worldbuilding consistency purposes.}}

The '''International dollar–US dollar tracking''' page models the exchange rate between the [[International dollar]] (XID), the currency of the [[Adonian Community]], and the real-world [[W:United States dollar|US dollar]] (USD). The model is used to maintain consistency between in-world economic figures (denominated in ID) and real-world equivalents, enabling meaningful comparisons of GDP, wages, prices, and other economic indicators across the fictional and real worlds.

== Model ==

=== Energy standard ===

The International dollar was introduced on 15 September 1948 under the [[Treaty of Calatayud]], initially pegged to fine gold. In 1952, the ID switched to an '''energy standard''', where 1 ID was defined as the cost to generate a fixed quantity of electricity at 1952 prices. The energy standard is based on the principle that energy, unlike gold or fiat currency, is governed by the laws of thermodynamics: it cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed or transferred. As energy production grows, the [[Adonian Monetary Authority]] (AMA) may expand the money supply without diluting the currency's value, because each unit of currency remains backed by a proportional share of the total energy base.

Under this system, approximately 4.57 ID = $1.00 USD in 1952. The ID has remained on the energy standard since 1952 and has never been a floating currency. The ID/USD exchange rate moves because the US dollar, a fiat currency since 1971, inflates and depreciates over time, while the ID's value remains anchored to the energy standard. The AMA expands the money supply in proportion to energy production growth, maintaining the currency's backing without devaluation.

=== Exchange rate formula ===

The ID/USD exchange rate is determined by the relative purchasing power of each currency. The ID remains pegged to the energy standard; the USD is fiat. The model calculates the rate as:

: ID/USD rate = Base rate × (USD cumulative inflation since 1952) / (ID cumulative inflation since 1952)

Where:
* '''Base rate''' = $0.2187 (1 ID = $0.2187 USD in 1952; calibrated so that 1 ID = $1.00 USD in 2015)
* '''USD cumulative inflation''' (''Earth context'') = US CPI-U (Bureau of Labor Statistics) ratio, 1952 to current year. This is real-world data reflecting the actual depreciation of the US dollar over time.
* '''ID cumulative inflation''' (''Adonia context'') = Modelled from the AMA's inflation target of "below, but close to, 2 per cent," with historical variation for actual in-world economic events. This is a fictional inflation series constructed for the worldbuilding.

The ID has appreciated against the USD because the energy standard constrains money creation to the growth of energy production, while the US dollar, as a fiat currency, has experienced higher average inflation.

=== ID inflation model ===

The ID's inflation rate is modelled year by year, reflecting the AMA's response to actual Adonia economic events. The only event that parallels a real-world event is the [[W:COVID-19 pandemic|COVID-19 pandemic]] (2020). All other events are specific to the Adonia world and have no direct real-world equivalent.

