The ID reached parity with the USD (1 ID = $1.00) in 2015, as the cumulative effect of the energy standard's lower inflation rate overtook the USD's higher fiat inflation. The ID briefly approached parity in 2008 during the global financial crisis, but the financial shock in Okaiken was averted and the ID did not sustain parity until 2015.

== Spot rate ==

The daily spot rate is generated by applying a simulated daily noise of ±0.5 per cent to the annual baseline rate, using a deterministic seed based on the date. This produces a stable, reproducible daily rate that fluctuates within a realistic band.

{| class="wikitable"
! Date !! 1 ID = USD !! 1 USD = ID !! Deviation from baseline
|-
| 2026-07-13 || $1.1766 || 0.8499 ID || +0.22%
|-
| 2026-07-20 || $1.1783 || 0.8487 ID || +0.36%
|-
| 2026-07-28 || $1.1723 || 0.8530 ID || -0.15%
|-
| 2026-07-31 || $1.1700 || 0.8547 ID || -0.35%
|}

The spot rate is updated daily by an automated script. The current baseline rate for 2026 is $1.1741 per ID.

== Implementation ==

The model is implemented as a Python script at <code>scripts/id_usd_tracker.py</code>. The script uses real-world US CPI data (''Earth context'') and a modelled ID inflation series (''Adonia context'') to compute the exchange rate. The ID inflation series reflects actual Adonia economic history, not real-world events. The only equivalent event between Adonia and Earth is the COVID-19 pandemic (2020). The script can generate historical rates, daily spot rates, and wiki table markup.

Usage:

 python3 scripts/id_usd_tracker.py --historical     # Print historical annual rates
 python3 scripts/id_usd_tracker.py --spot            # Generate today's spot rate
 python3 scripts/id_usd_tracker.py --wiki             # Generate wiki table markup

